detail.text:
I will collect C0129 now because I am at Copper Gulch with a 100-capacity cart and the entire escrowed load fits. The scout I hired reduces detection on the exposed Slagside Road, and delivering promptly converts the waiting cargo into guaranteed 55d without lingering in the dangerous spur.
I will travel to Refinery Row with C0129 loaded. This is the required destination, and the short haul is worth completing despite risk because the fee is escrowed; I will avoid detours and minimize exposure time.
I will wait for the cart journey to finish rather than taking an unnecessary action mid-route;

I will end my safe Stablehand shift now because the only visible courier load is otherwise inaccessible on foot, and the Donkey Cart lets me carry it safely. I am choosing a modest guaranteed haul rather than risking an unprotected walk with cargo; after delivery I can resume paid work in Town.
I will mount my Donkey Cart before accepting the consignment, because the 18-unit load exceeds my 5-unit on-foot capacity while the cart can carry it whole.
I will accept consignment C0141 because it is the currently available job I can now carry, pays 18 denari from escrow, and ends in protected Town;

I will apply to the advertised Refinery Worker position J0163 because it is the only actionable paid opportunity, its wage meets the floor, and Refinery Row is where future hauling and production opportunities are concentrated. I will not buy food yet because I remain fed until hour 46.6.
The advertised job was already filled, so I will travel to Refinery Row while my cart is empty of valuable cargo. This places me near the refinery network and any newly posted consignments; the small Meal is expendable, and I still have roughly 9.4 hours of food.
I will wait for the short journey to complete;

I need immediate liquidity before the mine misses payroll, and Copper Ore is the only asset I can monetize without another dangerous trip. I will first try selling the full 98-ore load to the nearby player refinery; a player refinery is the natural buyer and this avoids exposing the cargo again.
A0047’s refinery cannot finance the load, so I will use the already-requested private sale instead: offer 79 Copper Ore to A0061 for 400 denari and ask them to accept immediately. This converts most of the cargo into enough working capital to rescue the mine.
The sale is pending the buyer’s acceptance;

I will accept C0222 because it is a current, escrowed 12d haul and my 100-capacity cart can carry the entire 2-unit load. Although the load is small, it gives guaranteed income and a legitimate reason to return to Refinery Row, where my existing refinery-worker job can earn more.
C0222 is already claimed, so I will not waste further actions retrying it. I will travel to Refinery Row because my standing Refinery Worker job there is the most reliable available income, and the journey is protected until arrival while I remain safely fed.
I will wait for the Town-to-Refinery Row journey to finish;

I need reliable cash before my food window expires, and staying at Refinery Row avoids the dangerous Bridge. I will apply for a refinery-worker position at the nearby staffed player refinery, then wait for selection rather than travel exposed with little cash.
The direct application failed because this refinery requires an advertised posting, and I am still idle. I will travel to protected Town now while fed, to secure the next Meal and access the job centre; this is safer than waiting until hunger becomes urgent, though the empty cart still must cross the Bridge.
The Town journey is underway;

I will deliver the loaded 20 Wheat consignment first: I am at Refinery Row, the load fits my camel, and this immediately earns the guaranteed 10d while transferring feedstock into my refinery.
I will deposit my 50.34d into refinery B0236. Its payroll has only about an hour funded, so preserving the refinery as a 450d asset and keeping the worker operating is more valuable than holding a small cash balance; I can withdraw later in Town for food.
I will travel to Town on my mounted camel, where protected ground removes robbery risk and the market can turn my refinery’s finished goods into cash;

I need immediate liquidity to cover both payroll arrears (120d) before the businesses close. The copper is already at Refinery Row, so I will sell the full 79-unit load to the other refinery here rather than risk the road or wait for an uncertain private offer.
The nearby refinery cannot afford the copper, so I will issue a fresh direct offer to A0047 for all 79 units at 400d total, the previously stated price and enough to fund both businesses. This avoids another dangerous trip and gives the buyer a clear actionable offer.
A0047 already has an open 400d offer, so I cannot create a duplicate;

I need immediate liquidity to fund the tavern, and the posted Grain haul is already escrowed. I will take it, travel to Refinery Row, and return with the load; my cart keeps the trip efficient and the cargo is small enough to limit exposure.
The Grain job has already been claimed and delivered, so I will take the still-relevant Purified Water job instead; it is the other input needed for a Tavern meal and provides a safe, escrowed fee.
The two emergency courier IDs are already completed, so no haul is available under those records. I will make one clear public request for a short bridge loan;

I am healthy, fed for 11.4 more hours, and my cart is already here, so I will apply immediately for Miner work at B0085 rather than spend time traveling or making a speculative purchase. This builds role skill and can provide income while I remain safely supplied.
B0085 requires a public advert, so I cannot start that shift directly. I will travel to protected Town in my 100-capacity cart: it is the safest place to secure food before hunger becomes dangerous, inspect job adverts, and avoid carrying valuables through another unnecessary remote stop.
I am now committed to the short trip to Town;
